1785544625768564	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7AQ		item.comment	bn-3hkk	{"body":"RFC 0030 expanded 79 -> 413 lines: full normative spec. Structure: Status (normative IDL + companion RFCs + landed epoch.rs vocabulary + explicit draft-frontier disclaimer for research/27), Summary, Versioning and revision (five closed sets, fail-closed on unknown tokens, function_version rules, index-format versioning, epoch-advance demotion via Compatibility), Query key (typed 5-component table + 'which epochs enter the key' table over EpochKind::ALL, protocol epoch never, engine identity never), Query definition registry, Reuse-edge classes (closed 4-member table + trust order + meet rule + 5 downgrade rules), Reuse evidence (closed 5-form table), Nine dependency reasons (wire tokens mapped to plan 9.4 bullets) + reverse-direction agreement table with RFC 0031's impact mapping, Independence tri-state and invalidation-cone contract, Auditability classes (3 closed, INV-010 per class), Persistence/crash-safety/fsck, Incremental Parity Audit (sampling, 7 compared artifacts, 4-step mismatch procedure, quarantine triple, overhead), Proof/certificate freshness (defines the G5 'freshness is tracked' predicate), Continuations and epoch resume (what a continuation pins, resume-decision error table, first_mismatch contract), Wire surface, Formal model, Corrections, Flags, Rejected alternatives, Open questions, Acceptance.\n\n14 corrections recorded with direction. Highlights: (1) budget is NOT key material - RFC corrects plan 9.2 and docs/42 signatures explore(...,budget)/compile_context(...,budget); (2) query key carries consumed_epochs (restricted EpochSet), not just semantic+proof - RFC corrects its own earlier key against epoch.rs; (3) no checker epoch and no solver epoch exist - plan 9.2 check_certificate(certificate, checker_epoch), plan 9.4 'solver encoding epoch' and docs/42 'solver epoch' corrected; checker identity is the proof epoch or engine identity, solver encoding is strategy_config; (4,5) IDL governs the three query.* shapes - explain_invalidation is keyed by DiffHandle not (key, edit), and clean_compare is @mutation @task_starting not an 'ordinary read'; (6) plan 8.6 (and RFC 0032's restatement) wrongly call a Conservative disjointness judgement a Validated edge - corrected to Conservative unless a checkable witness exists; (9) docs/42's '1 in 64' is a labeled bootstrap default, NOT ratified - the research/27 register row stays draft, untouched; plus quarantine-triple scoping, G5-vs-9.5 reconciliation, 'Complete' is not a class, 11-vs-9 reason tokens, one class set with two names, 'dirty lane' names nothing, and INV-010's condition stated in full (not weakened).\n\nCross-artifact agreements: RFC 0031's dependency-reason mapping reproduced in reverse and declared MUST-agree; 'Unknown is dependent', 'heuristic independence only on Experimental', and 'Experimental never supports promotion' kept token-identical with RFC 0031; RFC 0031's classifier-identity clause satisfied (classifier version = function_version, CPNF version in strategy_config). epoch.rs: EpochSet::first_mismatch semantics (unpinned constrains nothing, first kind in EpochKind::ALL order, pinned-but-absent is a mismatch) written into the resume-decision table, plus the new normative rule that the CONTINUATION PINNING OBLIGATION is what makes that permissive rule safe.\n\n7 flags raised (nothing outside this RFC edited): F1 clean_compare's bare parity Bool cannot express the INV-008 distinctions; F2 reasons/edges are free-form strings vs INV-003; F3 no handle for an unmaterialized query key; F4 reuse evidence has no wire shape; F5 freshness has no wire home despite G5; F6 EpochSet::first_mismatch cannot check engine identity while RFC 0026/IDL require continuations to pin it (daemon must compose two predicates - obligation undeclared in both artifacts); F7 query-definition registry has no schema.\n\nFences respected: no edits to RFC 0026, RFC 0031/0037, schemas/*, or the section-25 ledger; plan.md untouched, so no traceability regeneration was needed. Validator: uv run --with jsonschema python3 tools/validate_dossier.py -> 'status': 'pass', program_status 'ready'; validation-results.json and VALIDATION_REPORT.md unmodified (git status shows only the RFC). Committed 3f7dbfa in .maw/workspaces/bn-3hkk. Not merged, not pushed, bone state unchanged."}	blake3:2IVN6taH1FC_JWa2bE1ZNfz3R68S6H83Nd_LsCAQUhs
1785544663584647	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7QQ		item.comment	bn-1ee03	{"body":"Done in workspace bn-1ee03 (commit ae2332e), not merged, no bone-state change.\n\nJUSTFILE: new 'lean' recipe = 'cd lean && lake build' then 'sh lean/scripts/axiom-manifest.sh --check'; wired into the chain as 'check: fmt-check lint test boundaries dossier lean'. Tool discovery is a plain PATH lookup of 'lake' (an elan proxy) — no elan path, no toolchain path, no mise invocation hardcoded, so a mise-exposed elan or ~/.elan/bin both work. If 'lake' is absent the recipe exits 1 with the bootstrap spelled out (mise install, then elan-init -y, then put elan's bin dir on PATH); verified by running 'just lean' with a PATH lacking ~/.elan/bin.\n\nMISE LAYERING FINDING (worth a follow-up bone): 'mise install' alone does NOT give you elan. The pinned github:leanprover/elan release asset is 'elan-init' (the installer), so mise puts only 'elan-init' on PATH — 'mise exec -- command -v elan' and 'mise which elan' both come up empty on this host. The working layering is mise, then elan-init, then ~/.elan/bin (elan/lake/lean), then lean/lean-toolchain. Root README's bootstrap block claimed 'mise install' installs elan itself and still named the removed 'ubi' backend; corrected both and added the 'elan-init -y' step. That is why the recipe's error text names 'mise install' AND 'elan-init', not 'mise install' alone.\n\nMANIFEST SCRIPT: fixed rather than documented. '--check' now runs the generator with a scratch directory as its working directory (the generator writes 'artifacts/...' relative to cwd), via 'MANIFEST_OUT_DIR=... MANIFEST_SRC=... lake env sh -c \"cd ... && exec lean ...\"' — quote-safe, and AxiomManifest.lean is unchanged — then diffs scratch against checked-in. lean/artifacts/ is read-only under --check now. For the record: the old script did copy the originals back after regenerating in place, so bn-zr81's \"overwrites before exiting 1\" was a transient window rather than a permanent clobber — but it churned the checked-in files on every run and left them overwritten if interrupted between generate and restore. Verified both paths: happy path exits 0 with a clean 'git status'; an artificially staled artifact exits 1, prints the diff, and the injected marker is still present afterwards (proving no rewrite).\n\nautoImplicit=false FALLOUT: none. Set via a package-level [leanOptions] table in lean/lakefile.toml. 'lake clean && lake build' from scratch: 19 jobs, no errors, no warnings, no sorry. Zero binders touched, zero .lean files changed — the tree already declares every universe/type variable explicitly. Because \"no fallout\" is a suspicious result I proved the option is actually in force: all 17 module setup.json files under .lake/build/ir carry options.autoImplicit = false, and a control file 'def probe (a : α) : α := a' errors under -DautoImplicit=false (\"not possible to treat α as an implicitly bound variable\") while compiling fine by default. Manifest preserved: regenerated output is byte-identical to both checked-in artifacts, theoremCount 68 and theoremsWithAxioms 0, so the zero-axiom property still holds. No sorry, no axiom, no weakened statement — the diff contains no Lean source changes at all.\n\nVERIFY: 'just check' passes end to end in the workspace (exit 0, run twice, lean recipe last). 'just lean' run twice back to back — both exit 0 and 'git status' is clean after (idempotent). Docs updated: lean/README.md (the two now-false \"wiring into just check remains an open follow-up\" claims, plus notes on autoImplicit and the read-only --check), README.md (toolchain bootstrap), AGENTS.md (the one line listing what 'just check' gates). Did not touch notes/, .bones/, crates/, mise.toml.\n\nCONCERNS: (1) the elan-init gap above — mise.toml's comment and bn-1rxrr's report both read as if mise provides elan itself; someone should decide whether to add a mise task/postinstall or keep the two-step bootstrap. (2) The dispatch brief said 78 theorems across 17 Lean files; the manifest actually has 68 theorems, and there are 17 .lean files under lean/ (16 in Continuum/ plus Continuum.lean), matching lean/README.md — nothing is missing, the 78 was a miscount. (3) AxiomManifest.lean sits outside the lean_lib target, so it is still elaborated with the Lake default autoImplicit; I confirmed it compiles clean under -DautoImplicit=false but left the flag off so 'lake env lean AxiomManifest.lean' (the invocation documented in lean/README.md) behaves identically however it is run. (4) On a host that has elan but not leanprover/lean4:v4.32.1, the first 'just lean' triggers an elan toolchain download — expected, but it makes the first 'just check' on a fresh machine slow rather than broken."}	blake3:gBaRHP2qN3-p1704nsZmA7Hrs5e8NsJI016tGAMOGkQ
1785544672974947	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7gQ		item.move	bn-3hkk	{"state":"done"}	blake3:xY-B3V0oB9NULOGBiZbxvzhfbHq27wBDtG13MMvASu8
1785544690348751	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy7wQ		item.create	bn-2ryko	{"description":"From bn-3hkk: (1) RFC 0032 restates plan §8.6's error verbatim — a Conservative disjointness judgement licensing a Validated reuse edge; Validated requires a checkable witness for the input digest (RFC 0030 'Reuse-edge classes'). Fix the sentence when RFC 0032 expands, or as a one-line correction sooner. (2) docs/42:105 says a disagreement 'quarantines the reuse class' — RFC 0030 scopes quarantine to the (class, function_id, function_version) triple; tighten the informal restatement.","kind":"task","title":"docs: RFC 0032 Validated-edge sentence and docs/42 quarantine scoping (one-line fixes from RFC 0030 expansion)"}	blake3:vsqp-mx-rPq9qaq2e1Up5RVx7g-elbkqtrrZv8g1sOQ
1785544690387088	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy8AQ		item.comment	bn-1bf	{"body":"From RFC 0030 expansion (bn-3hkk), flag F6 for the RFC 0026 expansion: epoch.rs scopes itself to the six compatibility epochs and declares engine identity out of scope, while RFC 0026 and the IDL EpochSet.engine require continuations to pin engine identity — so EpochSet::first_mismatch alone cannot validate a resume; the daemon must compose two predicates, and that obligation is currently undeclared in both artifacts. Declare it when expanding RFC 0026."}	blake3:v8TYjEDAdEqJT7AhZnWKkcvouYdRmdkHOq52U0e62NY
