1785545233381751	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhAU		item.comment	bn-3ffu	{"body":"Lead scope notes for the expansion: (1) F6 from RFC 0030 (bn-3hkk): epoch.rs first_mismatch covers the six compatibility epochs only, while RFC 0026/IDL EpochSet.engine requires continuations to pin engine identity — declare the two-predicate composition obligation. (2) The capability-administration operations gap (IDL open item 1 / RFC 0026 open question 1) — resolve or explicitly re-scope. (3) The IDL (schemas/continuumd-native-protocol.idl) is normative and freshly landed — expand the RFC to agree with it, corrections recorded with direction; SD-09's absorbed wire slice in the RFC is current, build on it."}	blake3:ZrKVUBKCWuU3YFk-ohDHvMJNnhR8JSG9tiBUvT8GBwo
1785545248195416	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhQU		item.comment	bn-3i38	{"body":"Lead scope note: fold in bn-2ryko item 1 — RFC 0032 restates plan §8.6's error (a Conservative disjointness judgement licensing a Validated reuse edge); RFC 0030's Reuse-edge classes section is normative — Validated requires a checkable witness for the input digest. Correct the sentence as part of the expansion and record the direction."}	blake3:MKJqweVz6fjvXRD8RsMRE6SpfJkZsdDLQRWvg5jTS6o
1785546063159973	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhgU		item.comment	bn-277	{"body":"ADR-0013 content identity landed in crates/continuum-value/src/identity.rs (1802 lines, +2 lib.rs doc/module lines); 29 new tests, just check green end to end (fmt, clippy -D warnings, tests, boundaries, dossier, lean).\n\nSemantics. Certified lane: ContentIdentity IS the CVNF-1 canonical encoding (Box<[u8]>), not a digest of it — no type parameter, no hasher argument, no field a hash can reach, so the certified equality relation is structurally independent of the hash-vendor decision. PartialEq is canonical byte comparison; Ord is byte order (= Value's Ord, which value.rs already pins). from_canonical_bytes decodes, so a store fetch re-derives identity from bytes rather than trusting the digest it asked for (ADR-0013 'proof validity still derives from decoded structure'). IdentityIndex<H> is ADR-0013's 'hashes index and partition; collisions resolve by exact comparison' made executable: BTreeMap<Digest256, Vec<ContentIdentity>>, bucket by digest, membership by canonical comparison; Insertion::Fresh{hash_collisions}/Existing reports collisions as data (INV-008: never a bare boolean).\n\nMode split as types. HashIdentity (digest+algorithm equality) cannot be built without a NonCertifiedLabel taken by value — no Default, no From<&str>, no From<ContentIdentity> (that conversion is an INV-011 assurance downgrade, so it is absent rather than convenient). Display is '<label>/<algorithm>:<digest>', so the weaker guarantee survives into any log line. Identity{Certified,NonCertified} never compare equal across modes.\n\nHash seam. trait ContentHasher { const ALGORITHM: HashAlgorithm; fn hash(&[u8]) -> Digest256 }. Placeholder = Fnv1aPlaceholder: four domain-separated FNV-1a lanes, token 'placeholder-fnv1a-256', HashAlgorithm::is_cryptographic() == false — the label is in-band, so any artifact recording the algorithm records the word 'placeholder'. Docs state plainly it has nothing like 256-bit collision resistance. Swapping in a vendored hash is a type substitution; it changes zero certified identities. Stdlib only, no new deps.\n\nCollision injection. Three adversarial test hashers (ConstantHash — everything collides; KindTagHash — same-kind collides; LengthHash — same-length collides) plus the placeholder. Proven under total collision: distinct values keep distinct identities, equal values coalesce to one (Insertion::Existing via three different routes incl. encode->decode round trip), a colliding lookup returns no false hit, collisions are counted not absorbed, and all four hashers give identical certified answers. docs/19 §7 hash-seed dimension is discharged at its strongest: sorted_identities() is byte-identical under different hash *functions* and under reversed/rotated insertion order. Non-certified side: under ConstantHash two distinct values do become one HashIdentity — demonstrated, and only reachable through a validated label.\n\nPlacement. continuum-value alongside value.rs: plan §20's dependency rules state ADR-0013 about this crate; an identity IS Value::encode bytes so any other home either adds a dependency edge or duplicates the encoding (two spellings of one identity — the failure the ADR prevents); docs/33 puts content identity in the smallest trust base; it is the only declared leaf crate, so cost is zero new edges. No plan §20 argument against.\n\nScope. Atomic publication and authorization untouched (bn-210) — documented seam: IdentityIndex::insert is the in-memory idempotent core, minus atomicity/durability/authorization. Digest256::to_token is 64 lowercase hex, asserted to sit inside artifact_path.rs's [A-Za-z0-9_-] identity class (asserted, not imported — leaf crate). value.rs/epoch.rs/assurance.rs/notes/.bones untouched.\n\nConcerns. (1) Placeholder digest golden vectors are pinned for determinism and are expected to change when the real hash lands; certified identity vectors are pinned separately and changing those is a plan §4.6 epoch event. (2) Digest256 is a public type, so nothing at the language level stops a caller from keying a set by digest and calling it identity — the docs say a digest is never an identity on its own, but that one is convention, not types. (3) Pre-existing unrelated rustdoc warning in assurance.rs:232 (broken intra-doc link AssuranceChange::Incomparable) — in the do-not-touch set, and cargo doc is not part of just check, so left alone."}	blake3:d8NA2CJWlYuZ7IAGbcdKyEFIMdtafpw292DcNnfOlgs
1785546104581031	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhwU		item.move	bn-277	{"state":"done"}	blake3:XE1I5z15HjDDGdIETc278R31UfdKouV8KYZP1owGVgA
1785546366327291	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyiAU		item.comment	bn-210	{"body":"Implemented in .maw/workspaces/bn-210 (commit 51599ca), just check green end to end.\n\nDELIVERED — crates/continuum-workspace/src/publication.rs (2719 lines incl. tests), lib.rs placement justification.\n\nState machine (types): stage -> commit_content -> commit_index, each transition consuming its predecessor. Content-before-index (docs/35 SD-09) is encoded in the API shape, not in prose: commit_index is a method on CommittedContent, and StagedPublication::commit_content is its only constructor. A compile_fail doctest checks that skipping the content commit does not compile, paired with an identical passing doctest so the setup cannot rot silently. Dropping either intermediate state is the modeled crash: dropping CommittedContent leaves exactly docs/35's residue (unreachable content, never a stale index entry), classified by StoreAudit::fsck in docs/35's three defect classes and reclaimed by collect_garbage. Every failure is PublicationAborted (RFC 0026): no index entry, no receipt, nothing truncated.\n\nConvergence: first publisher wins the index entry, later identical publications converge to the SAME identity, all receipts appended to an append-only ledger. Byte-different content under one identity aborts with IdentityCollision rather than conflating (ADR-0013 exact comparison, store side). Identity itself is an opaque ContentIdentifier trait parameter — bn-277/continuum-value untouched, no dependency edge added.\n\nPossession-independence (type-enforced, not documented): CapabilityDenied is a unit struct — zero bits — and read returns Result<Vec<u8>, CapabilityDenied>, so a distinct not-found is UNREPRESENTABLE for present and absent artifacts alike. AccessRequest carries no store reference and no existence bit, so an AuthorizationPolicy structurally cannot be an oracle; authorization always runs before the index is touched; an authorized read of an absent artifact is also denied (fail-closed keeps the refusal uniform). PublicationCost is a function of the request alone and the receipt carries no first-or-converged flag, so dedup is invisible in cost (RFC 0026). CapabilityToken cannot be built from a content-addressed handle; its Debug elides the secret. Every decision, permit and deny, goes to an AuditSink at decision time, naming no outcome.\n\nTests (46 unit + 4 doc, green in debug and release, 25x repeat of the concurrency tests with no flake): the DX-13 exit test runs 16 threads x 8 rounds publishing identical content and asserts one identity, 16 receipts from 16 distinct actors, one index entry, identical cost, empty fsck, and a schedule-independent store summary across all rounds — assertions on outcomes only, never on interleavings. Plus: concurrent distinct publications stay distinct; abort at each phase leaves nothing observable; denied reads are equal values (and equal Debug/Display) for present vs absent; the same denied request audits identically before and after publication; a leaked handle with no capability opens nothing.\n\nNOT DONE, needs the lead: the acceptance criterion's dossier half — flipping the G0-DX-13 row in notes/plan/notes/G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md and the plan §0.3 counts — was fenced out of this bone's workspace rules (do not touch notes/). It is a separate validator-enforced change and must land before the criterion reads as met."}	blake3:GTf3HCVn6tdLCuvAiT42Tisb_nut-gO-9qlEVBwMPXk
1785546416997507	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyiQU		item.move	bn-210	{"state":"done"}	blake3:FujqL_jmUa55AnsUpwJa1yshdUMZhdTfvhmdAzhZ8uc
1785546463611002	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyigU		item.comment	bn-3i38	{"body":"RFC 0032 expanded from 90-line summary to a 407-line normative specification (PR-0 form: field types, closed enums, versioning, RFC-2119), committed in .maw/workspaces/bn-3i38 as bc8d9ae. Validator: \"status\": \"pass\", SD-10 still the only open debt, SD-04 still paid; no schema/IDL/plan/ledger edits.\n\nStructure: Status header (both normative schemas + IDL vocabulary + claim_status.rs as landed vocabulary + FR-05 frontier dependency) / Summary / Versioning and revision (closed sets; version-is-lineage-not-schema-identity per SD-08) / transaction object field table / status machine with a total 8-rule derivation / operations with totality and idempotency / the twelve gates with per-gate rules / gate-status semantics + evidence discipline against the §11.4 lattice / gate profiles / neighborhood (8 closed strategy tokens + ratified FR-05 quote and counting rule) / mutation challenge / cost governance / reclassification / concurrency and lineage / promotion incl. rollback / receipt composition / 14 Corrections + 9 Flags (RFC 0031 pattern) / rejected alternatives / open questions / acceptance test vectors.\n\nLead-noted correction applied as Correction 1: the 'Incremental gate campaigns' bullet no longer says a Conservative disjointness judgement licenses a Validated reuse edge. Normative now: Conservative licenses Conservative; Validated only with an independently checkable witness for the input digest; Unknown disjointness re-runs; Experimental never supports promotion (meet rule). Direction recorded: RFC 0030 owns the closed reuse-edge class set and already recorded this against plan §8.6 and against RFC 0032 (its correction 6, 'MUST be revised to match') — RFC 0032 is corrected to agree with RFC 0030; plan §8.6 stands corrected by RFC 0030, not by this RFC.\n\nOther corrections with direction: (2) repair.begin takes {failure, gate_profile} only, not (failure, base, intent) — IDL decides; (3) stale-base promotion is StatusConflict, not StaleSnapshot — StaleSnapshot is not in any repair.* union under rule errors.common; (4) gate_profile declared at begin and frozen; (5) NotYetEnforced is prose, not_yet_enforced is the token; (6) gate 1 failed (no reproduction) vs inconclusive + defect_* (ReplayDiverged) — governs docs/41; (7) gate 8's 'unexpectedly' made a predicate; (8) gate 3 passes on the recomputed allow verdict, not on the phrase; (9) per-transaction ceiling = BudgetExhausted + continuation vs per-principal = QuotaExhausted — RFC 0026 taxonomy governs plan §8.6's collapse; (10) receipt's semantic_diff and intent_diff must name the same diff_* (RFC 0031 one-artifact rule); (11) receipt MUST carry policy_decision/coverage/unknowns though the schema makes them optional; (12) hypothesis and §8.4 counterfactuals are never evidence; (13) plan §8.5's single neighborhood number is a rendering; (14) docs/41's struct is not the artifact shape (SD-10).\n\nAgreements: gate name/status/profile enums, the twelve-gate identity rule, the profile conditionals, the promoted conditional, the 5+4 cost dimensions, and only passed/not_yet_enforced on a receipt all reconcile one-to-one with the two schemas; gate 12 pending on ready matches the shipped example. Lattice: gate statuses and claim statuses kept as separate vocabularies sharing only 'inconclusive'; evidence floor stated over the observed..proved band (refuted/superseded sit above proved in the chain without being stronger assurance); no-regression + StatusConflict cited to claim_status.rs. FR-05: the ratified sentence is quoted verbatim (checked byte-identical to research/33) and its counting rule made normative — an undisclosed failing neighbor is not a catch, so gate 5 fails; no adequacy claim until the Phase B corpus lands.\n\nConcerns for the schema/protocol sweeps (flags F1-F9): coverage has no machine shape, so the failing-neighbor disclosure the ratified threshold depends on has nowhere typed to live (F8); reuse-edge class/function_version are unrecorded in the receipt, so Correction 1's distinction is unauditable (F9); repair.apply and repair.evaluate have no typed lifecycle-refusal code (F1); policy_verdict optional at every status (F6); version/supersedes untied (F5); untyped performance_impact/security_review/evaluation_policy (F3); duplicated semantic_epoch and dual diff fields (F7)."}	blake3:zwqiPOZqHBsCx7_SJzlzsFxP7RFkqtG9JeVm-oPGj5k
1785546533528282	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyiwU		item.move	bn-3i38	{"state":"done"}	blake3:G-UJE1u_UXW4a0UOhCzp6bFF9GAT9g0TxFB8uOCnOE4
1785546533780468	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyjAU		item.comment	bn-1lfek	{"body":"RFC 0032 expansion (bn-3i38) adds receipt-schema gaps for the same sweep: F8 coverage is untyped (additionalProperties:true) so the ratified FR-05 failing-neighbor disclosure has no typed home and cannot be graded mechanically; F9 no field records reuse-edge class/function_version of reused gate results, so the Conservative-vs-Validated distinction is unauditable from a receipt; F1 repair.apply/evaluate lack a typed lifecycle-refusal code. Full flag list in RFC 0032's Flags section."}	blake3:_5XEziVoQ0IFdwucmv7z5BDulQeDOLuj9rU_MaTxoM0
1785546597192780	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyjQU		item.comment	bn-4xxw	{"body":"RFC 0028 expanded from summary (80 lines) to normative spec (320 lines), committed in .maw/workspaces/bn-4xxw as efb05f9. Structure: header (normative schema + IDL vocabulary + companion sources + landed vocabulary + ratified frontier dependency), Summary, Versioning and revision, Pack identity/lineage/determinism, Required fields reconciled one-to-one with plan 6.2's fourteen bullets, Verdict and assurance, Guarantee classes (13-member table + rules C1-C6), Selection and causal core, ten-stage compiler pipeline table, Budgets and packing (incl. the pack's frontier form for RFC 0030 budget-sensitivity), Omission manifest (exact-count reconciliation equation), Expansion protocol (closed ExpansionRelation + typed-outcome table incl. redacted/purged and budget shortfall), Redaction and privacy, four pack profiles (failure/reachability/invariant/proof-target), Views and rendering, Wire surface, Incremental and evidence-graph interaction, Validation, Formal model, 15 numbered Corrections with direction, 12 Flags, Rejected alternatives, Open questions, Acceptance. Key corrections: target-gate metadata (proof profile feeds G6, not replay preservation); ExpansionRelation is closed and the shipped example's 'omitted_noise_events' is non-conformant; bytes are the recorded budget; docs/38's ExplanationIncomplete is not an ErrorCode/InconclusiveReason (maps to inconclusive + typed reason); ExplanationMinimal needs study evidence not a minimizer transcript; plan 6.2's list is the failure profile only; heuristic segregation made structural (schema has no per-item guarantee field); semantic_epoch scoping rule; plan 15.2's allowed tactics/axioms are not pack content; G0-DX-01's 23.62x is artifact-shape evidence only (docs/53). Ratified FR-01: no numbers restated, and the 'counting every expansion' clause is turned into an explicit lineage obligation (F1) since the artifact has no parent field. Fences respected: no edits to other RFCs, schemas/*.json, the IDL, plan.md, or the 25 ledger. Validator: notes/plan tools/validate_dossier.py -> status pass, program_status ready; validation-results.json and VALIDATION_REPORT.md untouched."}	blake3:Cx7EW6JAs-Q9brPqVAcSbCrPxoYs02QEsFI1lYtFUjo
1785546650803169	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyjgU		item.move	bn-4xxw	{"state":"done"}	blake3:OCmSdq_m7LILkY7OLfc1YwJwGIb5R-4_hEwAlcKiwzc
1785546651058356	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyjwU		item.comment	bn-1lfek	{"body":"PRIORITY item from RFC 0028 (bn-4xxw): F1 — context-pack schema has no parent/lineage field (additionalProperties:false), so the ratified FR-01 metric 'counting every expansion' is UNCOMPUTABLE from artifacts alone; needs a parent-handle schema addition before the FR-01 ablation is scheduled. Also: schemas/examples/context-pack.example.json is now explicitly non-conformant with RFC 0028 on two schema-permitted counts (omitted_noise_events relation token, tokens-only budget) — regenerate in the sweep. Full flags F1-F12 in RFC 0028's Flags section; C4 interim segregation rule should be revisited once per-item guarantee attribution (F2) lands."}	blake3:P_7vJHkE8fqyNBTtmuCwTiyOaTvXjnRUcVvRyEjl2JE
1785546736031950	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykAU		item.comment	bn-3ffu	{"body":"RFC 0026 expanded to full normative specification (574 lines, +487/-74) in .maw/workspaces/bn-3ffu, committed 7b48e91. Validator: status pass (spec-debt open set unchanged: SD-10 only).\n\nStructure: Precedence (schemas > IDL > RFC > plan, plus an explicit rule for IDL-internal contradictions) / Versioning and revision (incl. version window and negotiation) / Connection lifecycle / Request envelope / Result envelope (verdicts, assurance envelope, cost and omissions) / Operation semantics (annotation obligations across all 72 ops, unshipped surface, adapter parity) / Ordering, idempotency, atomicity / Task lifecycle / Epochs on the wire (continuations and resume admissibility, epoch advance) / Error taxonomy / Operational contract on the wire (SD-09, preserved verbatim and extended) / Transport, encoding, authentication / Capability administration / Conformance and acceptance / 36 Corrections with direction / 13 Flags / Rejected alternatives / Open questions.\n\nLead scope note 1 - two-predicate obligation: declared under 'Continuations and resume admissibility'. Admissibility is P1 (EpochSet::first_mismatch over the six compatibility epochs == None) AND P2 (pinned.engine == current.engine); either disagreement yields ContinuationEpochMismatch. Phrasing is token-identical with RFC 0030's 'Resume decision' and closes RFC 0030's F6. Added decisions: the protocol epoch does NOT participate in resume (connection-scoped; a protocol-minor difference must not be ContinuationEpochMismatch - it is the handshake window and ProtocolVersionUnsupported), and engine is nullable on the wire but non-null in a continuation (rejected at creation). Required acceptance row: engine change with all six epochs matching must fail, since a one-predicate implementation passes every other resume test.\n\nLead scope note 2 - capability administration: RESOLVED as out-of-band for protocol major 3, closing IDL open item 1. Three reasons: no authority level on RFC 0027's five-rung ladder can hold a mint; a mint reachable from ClientHello.capability is a privilege-escalation surface (the protocol now states that no operation can widen the authority of the connection invoking it, INV-015); CapabilityDescriptor plus ServerWelcome.grant already fix the vocabulary. Non-conditional obligations restated (audit, sharing policy as capability property, grant as sole authority channel, revocation effective on in-flight connections and never retroactive, revocation-not-purge). IDL open item 2 also closed fail-closed: delegation_depth defaults 0, a delegated grant never exceeds its parent in level/scope/expiry/depth, expires_at null confined to a shared trust domain. No plan §10.2 or RFC 0027 edit; the registry edit a future reversal would need is flagged (F13).\n\nFences honoured: zero edits to the IDL, schemas/*.json, other RFCs, plan.md, the §25 ledger, validation-results.json, VALIDATION_REPORT.md. Only notes/plan/rfcs/0026-*.md changed.\n\nWire-side items found that need a lead decision (flagged, not patched): F5 task.resume/repair.resume errors clauses omit StaleSnapshot though rule task.resume requires it and errors.common does not supply it (RFC declares rule task.resume governs; minimal fix is adding the code to two clauses, a compatible change); F6 evidence.verify has no field able to carry a Redacted, so the SD-09 obligation is unimplementable as declared (minimal fix: one optional field); F7 no rule requires defect_* emission and program.replay returns no defect handle though ReplayDiverged is in its errors; F4/F12 IDL open items 1-2 now stale and ExplanationLevel misattributed to docs/55 (comment-only, should bump idl_version).\n\nAlso note for the owner: RFC 0030's F6 now reads slightly stale ('undeclared in both') since RFC 0026 declares the composition; RFC 0030 was not edited."}	blake3:3KjWztumhTX0mHJjXjci8vju5Opxz3WRtuAMAC_xNH0
1785546804023331	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykQU		item.move	bn-3ffu	{"state":"done"}	blake3:5Rd89r6G3cXROxKUfFNv_D35u5FZ8W97devrTJdwNW8
1785546804403903	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykgU		item.create	bn-2wu5j	{"description":"From bn-3ffu, wire-side defects the RFC flagged rather than patched (each needs a small deliberate IDL edit): F5 task.resume/repair.resume errors clauses omit StaleSnapshot though rule task.resume requires it; F6 evidence.verify response has no field able to carry a Redacted, making an SD-09 obligation unimplementable — add one optional field; F7 no rule requires defect_* emission and program.replay returns no defect handle despite ReplayDiverged; F4/F12 IDL open items 1-2 are stale (capability administration and delegation decided in RFC 0026) and the preamble misattributes ExplanationLevel (RFC 0039, not docs/55). Bump idl_version per the IDL's own versioning rules. Also: RFC 0030's F6 flag line now stale (says the composition obligation is undeclared in both artifacts; RFC 0026 declares it) — one-line update.","kind":"task","title":"chore: minimal IDL wire fixes from RFC 0026 expansion (F5/F6/F7, stale open items, idl_version bump)"}	blake3:6A6QS1ybF5oRIdP9AOVkpMWNZdu6Vz6WJ4Js2RrJh5Q
